Guard the term and value checkers' recursion against stack exhaustion

nano-lean checks every declaration against the declared types and values of the others,
including ones it rejected. A rejected declaration whose type or value refers to itself
sends a later declaration's checking into recursion without end, and nl-fast overflows
its 256 MiB worker stack on exports of a few hundred bytes:
- term core: infer -> infer_proj -> is_prop -> infer, and whnf -> whnf_core -> reduce_rec;
- value core: type_of through Pi domains; whnf -> reduce_nat -> nat_val -> whnf when a
  Nat primitive's operand unfolds to the same application; def_eq_core re-entering itself
  through whnf_core and lazy delta, past def_eq's guard.
The kernel, the value checker's eval/whnf_core and the inductive checker already decline at
a stack floor. This checks the floor in Tc::tick (every term-core step), Vc::type_of,
Vc::whnf (slow path) and Vc::def_eq_core, so such declarations decline with the stack budget.
Upstream: none (no issues/PRs upstream, checked 2026-11-22).

